      "text": "# REA Toolkit MCP connection for DeepSeek Harness.\n#\n# Resolution contract (first match wins):\n#   1. DSH_REA_NODE + DSH_REA_HOME set  -> absolute node + bundled REA runtime (offline, validated artifact).\n#   2. DSH_REA_HOME set only            -> \"node\" from PATH + bundled REA runtime.\n#   3. Neither set                      -> npx fetches the official rea-agents runtime from npm.\n#\n# Run install-tools.(bat|sh|mjs) once per workspace to provision (1) or (2); it\n# persists both variables at user scope and verifies the runtime with\n# `rea mcp doctor`. Restart DeepSeek Harness afterwards so the host process\n# inherits the variables. failOnStartupError stays false so an unprovisioned\n# workspace degrades to no REA tools instead of blocking harness boot.\n- insert:\n    - id: rea-toolkit-mcp\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client'\n      config:\n        serverName: rea\n        transport: stdio\n        command: !!js 'process.env.DSH_REA_NODE || (process.env.DSH_REA_HOME ? \"node\" : \"npx\")'\n        args: !!js 'process.env.DSH_REA_HOME ? [process.env.DSH_REA_HOME + \"/scripts/rea.mjs\", \"mcp\"] : [\"-y\", \"rea-agents@6.7.0\", \"mcp\"]'\n        failOnStartupError: false\n        toolCallTimeoutMs: 120000\n"
